      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "text": "False - use of patterns should be considered in context. \nIf small game, might be redundant or there might be another way. \nIf chess uses inheritance and a method already exists of \ntake(Piece: piece) than implementing observer is not needed. \n\nIf you had a scoreboard GUI that need to be updated, \nthen it may be justified\n",
      "baseline": 189,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "False - use of patterns should be considered in context. \nIf small game, might be redundant or there might be another way. \nIf chess uses inheritance and a method already exists of \ntake(Piece: piece) than implementing observer is not needed. \n\nIf you had a scoreboard GUI that need to be updated, \nthen it may be justified\n",
      "index": "aH",
