    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 835,
      "versionNonce": 292859793,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "6fbrP_V8Kg9oOjzRymHF5",
      "fillStyle": "hachure",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": -203.1644150975104,
      "y": 10344.707422976979,
      "strokeColor": "#364fc7",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 1387.6513671875,
      "height": 284,
      "seed": 1577339579,
      "groupIds": [],
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1748306670953,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "text": "What is a Lambda Function?\nA lambda function is a concise way to represent an anonymous function.\nThe Java compiler automatically decides which functional interface (any interface with exactly one \nabstract method) a lambda function must match.\n\nIntroduced in Java 8.\n\nSyntax: (parameters) -> expression",
      "baseline": 60,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "What is a Lambda Function?\nA lambda function is a concise way to represent an anonymous function.\nThe Java compiler automatically decides which functional interface (any interface with exactly one \nabstract method) a lambda function must match.\n\nIntroduced in Java 8.\n\nSyntax: (parameters) -> expression",
      "index": "b0b",
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.2678571428571428
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 280,
      "versionNonce": 796617873,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "1qySo_Lo22sQCxBZOC8SN",
      "fillStyle": "hachure",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": -189.60746762142782,
      "y": 10722.557634908915,
      "strokeColor": "#5c940d",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 807.127685546875,
      "height": 210,
      "seed": 1581333339,
      "groupIds": [],
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1748306788257,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "text": "Why Use Lambdas?\n\n- Enables functional programming in Java.\n- Reduces boilerplate code.\n- Commonly used with functional interfaces (like Runnable, \nComparator, Predicate).",
      "baseline": 25,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Why Use Lambdas?\n\n- Enables functional programming in Java.\n- Reduces boilerplate code.\n- Commonly used with functional interfaces (like Runnable, \nComparator, Predicate).",
      "index": "b0d",
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 637,
      "versionNonce": 1322102001,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "hkF8yZDki_vuRaWYQV-gx",
      "fillStyle": "hachure",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 878.2433399202155,
      "y": 10586.834805736571,
      "strokeColor": "#495057",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 326.979736328125,
      "height": 196.57142857142858,
      "seed": 235338709,
      "groupIds": [],
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1748306793373,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "text": "Without Lambda:\n\nRunnable r = new Runnable() {\n    public void run() {\n        System.out.println(\"Hello\");\n    }\n};\n",
      "baseline": 165,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Without Lambda:\n\nRunnable r = new Runnable() {\n    public void run() {\n        System.out.println(\"Hello\");\n    }\n};\n",
      "index": "b0e",
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.2285714285714286
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 441,
      "versionNonce": 148945791,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "sxc5jLm7oA1U87keuLqRN",
      "fillStyle": "hachure",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": -169.24539772437197,
      "y": 10973.607997493642,
      "strokeColor": "#c92a2a",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 874.7196655273438,
      "height": 245,
      "seed": 1993807867,
      "groupIds": [],
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1748306756922,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "text": "Why Can't We Just Use Lambda Functions Everywhere in Java?\n\n- Tied to Functional Interfaces\n- No State or Fields\n- Limited Readability for Complex Logic\n- No Overriding or Inheritance\n",
      "baseline": 25,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Why Can't We Just Use Lambda Functions Everywhere in Java?\n\n- Tied to Functional Interfaces\n- No State or Fields\n- Limited Readability for Complex Logic\n- No Overriding or Inheritance\n",
      "index": "b0f",
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 380,
      "versionNonce": 849312447,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "zpo-Xxm-IIPvl8zR4SqsL",
      "fillStyle": "hachure",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 873.9396483171347,
