      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "text": "What is a Java Variadic Method?\nA variadic method in Java is a method that accepts a variable number of arguments of the same type.",
      "baseline": 95,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "What is a Java Variadic Method?\nA variadic method in Java is a method that accepts a variable number of arguments of the same type.",
      "index": "b0k",
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.261904761904762
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
